The primary outcome is self-reported pain measured by VAS immediately after insertion, which is within the criteria's 
timeframe (up to six hours). The study design (RCT), intervention (NSAID for IUC insertion pain), comparator (placebo), 
and outcome (self-reported pain) all match the selection criteria. Therefore, INCLUDE.
Confidence: high.

